text.en:
These Regulations do not apply —

(a) to any liquid, aerosol or gel carried by one passenger in one or more containers with an individual capacity not exceeding 100 millilitres or its equivalent places within a single closed transparent re-sealable plastic bag of a maximum capacity not exceeding one litre;

(b) to any liquid, aerosol or gel purchased at an airport retail outlet or on board an aircraft during a flight if they —

(i) are carried in a security tamper-evident bag; and

(ii) have been protected from unlawful interference by a process of supply chain security, including the application of appropriate security measures at the places of manufacture and at warehouses, during the delivery process for both liquids, aerosols and gels and security tamper-evident bags from the warehouse to the airport retail outlets and aircraft outlets, and whilst in stock or on display at those outlets;

(c) to any medication, babies’ milk or food and any special dietary or other medical requirement which is needed during the flight, either for essential medical purposes or to meet any special and essential dietary needs;

(d) to flight crew in uniform and on duty during such a flight.
